cfff" :answer-field/id #uuid "f27420ae-18fa-5d0e-a580-5e1bf60bcfff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c5fd2a5f-63d4-5986-8bd2-0c3f040855b1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5fd2a5f-63d4-5986-8bd2-0c3f040855b1" "answer-546d53e9-7744-5f86-b876-fc80b81f7103" "answer-db61f163-b057-55c2-aae3-6225b5a73432" "answer-3915a727-70cd-5944-8e37-741313f3aab3" "answer-11677232-a03f-5db9-86bb-785e38f7012a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5fd2a5f-63d4-5986-8bd2-0c3f040855b1" :answer/id #uuid "c5fd2a5f-63d4-5986-8bd2-0c3f040855b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-546d53e9-7744-5f86-b876-fc80b81f7103" :answer/id #uuid "546d53e9-7744-5f86-b876-fc80b81f7103" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db61f163-b057-55c2-aae3-6225b5a73432" :answer/id #uuid "db61f163-b057-55c2-aae3-6225b5a73432" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt[3]{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3915a727-70cd-5944-8e37-741313f3aab3" :answer/id #uuid "3915a727-70cd-5944-8e37-741313f3aab3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11677232-a03f-5db9-86bb-785e38f7012a" :answer/id #uuid "11677232-a03f-5db9-86bb-785e38f7012a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt[3]{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7e8f9822-aefa-57f0-9acd-f132c358e3dc" :question/id #uuid "7e8f9822-aefa-57f0-9acd-f132c358e3dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-99612" :question/problem "$\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{216}{343}}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the fraction under the radical as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{216}{343}}=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{(-216)}{343}}\n$$\n\nThe cube root of a quotient of two numbers is equal to the quotient of the cube roots of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{(-216)}{343}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{-216}}{\\sqrt[3]{343}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{7} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{7}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9b41596b-ac3f-54ae-b6c0-acf538414639"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9b41596b-ac3f-54ae-b6c0-acf538414639" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b41596b-ac3f-54ae-b6c0-acf538414639" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-79c62a52-438b-5e92-ac3c-f33a5c6b7310" :answer-field/choices ["answer-95bc6fe6-fd25-5ef8-b18c-f21b73165355" "answer-79c62a52-438b-5e92-ac3c-f33a5c6b7310" "answer-5cc0ef03-dac6-5659-88ce-45047c68405d" "answer-eb7c7921-2c98-5e0e-8157-eff53fe358a1" "answer-27e57adc-f0b4-58e1-883b-dcf269211231"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95bc6fe6-fd25-5ef8-b18c-f21b73165355" :answer/id #uuid "95bc6fe6-fd25-5ef8-b18c-f21b73165355" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79c62a52-438b-5e92-ac3c-f33a5c6b7310" :answer/id #uuid "79c62a52-438b-5e92-ac3c-f33a5c6b7310" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cc0ef03-dac6-5659-88ce-45047c68405d" :answer/id #uuid "5cc0ef03-dac6-5659-88ce-45047c68405d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb7c7921-2c98-5e0e-8157-eff53fe358a1" :answer/id #uuid "eb7c7921-2c98-5e0e-8157-eff53fe358a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27e57adc-f0b4-58e1-883b-dcf269211231" :answer/id #uuid "27e57adc-f0b4-58e1-883b-dcf269211231" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186139644 :tutorial/content "To divide square roots, we simply divide the numbers under the root. This is called the **quotient rule for radicals**.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's simplify the expression $\\dfrac{ \\sqrt{10} }{ \\sqrt{2} }$ by applying the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{ \\sqrt{10} }{ \\sqrt{2} } = \\sqrt{ \\dfrac{10}{2} } = \\sqrt{5}\n$$\n\nThe quotient rule also works for cube roots. For example,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{ \\sqrt[3]{10} }{ \\sqrt[3]{2} } = \\sqrt[3]{ \\dfrac{10}{2} } = \\sqrt[3]{5}\n$$\n\nIn general, the quotient rule works for any quotient of $n$th roots. So for any $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{ \\sqrt[n]{10} }{ \\sqrt[n]{2} } = \\sqrt[n]{ \\dfrac{10}{2} } = \\sqrt[n]{5}.\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** We cannot use the quotient rule when we have the quotient of different radicals, such as square roots and cube roots. For example, the expression $\\dfrac{ \\sqrt{10} }{ \\sqrt[3]{5} }$ cannot be simplified because the radicals $\\sqrt{\\phantom{x}}$ and $\\sqrt[3]{\\phantom{x}}$ are different." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138594 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186173806 :answer-field/choices 17592186173808] [:db/retract 17592186173806 :answer-field/choices 17592186173809] [:db/retract 17592186173806 :answer-field/choices 17592186173810] [:db/retract 17592186173806 :answer-field/choices 17592186173811] [:db/retract 17592186173806 :answer-field/choices 17592186173807] [:db/retract 17592186174442 :answer-field/choices 17592186174443] [:db/retract 17592186174442 :answer-field/choices 17592186174444] [:db/retract 17592186174442 :answer-field/choices 17592186174445] [:db/retract 17592186174442 :answer-field/choices 17592186174446] [:db/retract 17592186174442 :answer-field/choices 17592186174447] {:db/id 17592186175999 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7462dbdf-074b-5e9c-88bb-4a4709315e55" "question-7040e2bd-4a32-5fec-9df4-e31bdd95ffae" "question-acc3ecee-2ca3-52a4-a564-fe35d9f4b095" "question-a1209ac5-9324-5c4f-8a14-c5d815ce9e79"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175852 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n![](images/95/95ded6d2fba38750193e0b88b6c957dd841203590c6ce6ad493b19c31c76ac0b.svg)\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF $f_Y(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\leq y \\leq1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{15}{7}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{7}{y}^{4}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}{y}^{4}[{x}^{3}]_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}{y}^{4}({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =5{y}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is given by\n\n![](images/14/140bdf82e603fcf61a0d217da56acd876bf97a88ef2f318e84a9477374ec3abe.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176000 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6d033f40-c93e-54e7-8136-01042b0b61b2" "question-aecec449-e3ae-5803-8a70-f99f6be91bad" "question-bdb3668b-11de-51d3-b228-d2e5f99dedeb" "question-335726b7-e5f3-5cb6-916f-382cd146373a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175853 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n![](images/a1/a1015cb8e8c7cd0bcee792c919b5f9c6f0e1ce180e971fcfeda8eecfc8238a47.svg)\nFind $P(-4 \\leq Y \\leq 4).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $y \\geq 0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(4x+y/4)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-(4x+y/4)}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\infty } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(0-{e}^{-(0+y/4)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-y/4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is given by\n\n![](images/81/810669e70e34a95f937272d35174b4ccc72a5a3d6356a322893e516e7b6f4597.svg)\n\nTherefore, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-4\\le Y\\le 4) & ={\\int }_{-4}^{4}{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-y/4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-y/4}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =(-{e}^{-4/4}+{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176037 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b503f4b2-2e6a-599e-9f9e-bfcbf92fe455"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175684 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = 5y\\sqrt{x},  \\quad y^2 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad y\\geq 0.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF $f_Y(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D = \\{(x,y) \\::\\:   y^2 \\leq x \\leq1,\\, y\\geq 0 \\}.$\n\n![](images/4c/4c689a61af43d1d7aef57364a0d231256329305438e3fa046b048b7580fc13fe.png)\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0 \\leq y \\leq 1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}5y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5y{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5y{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}]}_{x={y}^{2}}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10y}{3}{[{x}^{3/2}]}_{x={y}^{2}}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10y}{3}[{1}^{3/2}-{({y}^{2})}^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{10y}{3}[1-{y}^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{10(y-{y}^{4})}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is given by\n\n![](images/45/455169bc586c4c80c170a1ec5b8a831814f60e378ae56f471c0db75f439f6c36.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176001 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-076df80a-4584-5238-8a7e-ff37062cbf3b" "question-b66f8317-7401-5c42-a057-174f43015e08" "question-74d58075-0369-56a0-b633-ba74268879be" "question-4107781e-c996-571c-b9f1-cc16eec90a01" "question-31433c7d-56df-5a56-80c3-21c7e39be82f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175854 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n![](images/38/38fbcd9603e79b21eb176e030a66ddf8d6a7e9e000c81b39987fa743380b92ea.svg)\n\nFind the marginal cumulative distribution function (CDF) $F_Y(y)$ of $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $-1 \\leq y \\leq 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}(x+y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{[\\frac{1}{3}(x+y)^{3}]}_{x=-1}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[(x+y)^{3}]}_{x=-1}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[(1+y)^{3}-(-1+y)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[(y+1)^{3}-(y-1)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[({y}^{3}+3{y}^{2}+3y+1)-({y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}+3y-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[(\\cancel{{y}^{3}}+3{y}^{2}+\\cancel{3y}+1)-(\\cancel{{y}^{3}}-3{y}^{2}+\\cancel{3y}-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[2(3{y}^{2}+1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(3{y}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $Y$ for $-1 \\leq y \\leq 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{f}_{Y}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{y}\\frac{1}{4}(3{u}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{y}(3{u}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[{u}^{3}+u]}_{-1}^{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[{y}^{3}+y-(-1)^{3}-(-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[{y}^{3}+y+2] \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{3}+y+2}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the marginal CDF of $Y$ is\n\n![](images/0a/0a44179f2169e2c2660c6bb6e5bb23d5298786ee5d3f0fb181c3b71bf61ca0fe.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-7462dbdf-074b-5e9c-88bb-4a4709315e55" :question/id #uuid "7462dbdf-074b-5e9c-88bb-4a4709315e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-142872" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y), & 0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+y)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7fc4e10a-30c9-5bff-b8a6-df1e61c3c7b8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7fc4e10a-30c9-5bff-b8a6-df1e61c3c7b8" :answer-field/id #uuid "7fc4e10a-30c9-5bff-b8a6-df1e61c3c7b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eabdea2d-66a4-530f-bf9f-3cb5839040be" :answer-field/choices ["answer-96202c10-895a-5653-9141-10869b52646e" "answer-6e97b129-580d-59cf-b93d-a5f15b4a69f0" "answer-cb40a145-d832-5c0d-b590-7a7995459d68" "answer-a0ede3e4-6cd5-51ec-a66b-65ac756d3972" "answer-eabdea2d-66a4-530f-bf9f-3cb5839040be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96202c10-895a-5653-9141-10869b52646e" :answer/id #uuid "96202c10-895a-5653-9141-10869b52646e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-\\sqrt{2}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e97b129-580d-59cf-b93d-a5f15b4a69f0" :answer/id #uuid "6e97b129-580d-59cf-b93d-a5f15b4a69f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-\\sqrt{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb40a145-d832-5c0d-b590-7a7995459d68" :answer/id #uuid "cb40a145-d832-5c0d-b590-7a7995459d68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-\\sqrt{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0ede3e4-6cd5-51ec-a66b-65ac756d3972" :answer/id #uuid "a0ede3e4-6cd5-51ec-a66b-65ac756d3972" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eabdea2d-66a4-530f-bf9f-3cb5839040be" :answer/id #uuid "eabdea2d-66a4-530f-bf9f-3cb5839040be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176258 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $1\\le y\\le 2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}y{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}y[{x}^{4}]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}y({1}^{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}y, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173806 :answer-field/correct "answer-6d3e17cd-c3c8-537b-b290-5a1e7b10eed5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2852486-2a3e-5a1c-8255-69aa2ae0c1fc" "answer-920faada-7711-5c7e-870a-65e8a1d7f033" "answer-6d3e17cd-c3c8-537b-b290-5a1e7b10eed5" "answer-0df9164a-2aee-5ef0-b081-85127f1a8451" "answer-1c514f66-29f0-5f0b-bfe0-72c4620d0193"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2852486-2a3e-5a1c-8255-69aa2ae0c1fc" :answer/id #uuid "b2852486-2a3e-5a1c-8255-69aa2ae0c1fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-920faada-7711-5c7e-870a-65e8a1d7f033" :answer/id #uuid "920faada-7711-5c7e-870a-65e8a1d7f033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}y, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d3e17cd-c3c8-537b-b290-5a1e7b10eed5" :answer/id #uuid "6d3e17cd-c3c8-537b-b290-5a1e7b10eed5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}y, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0df9164a-2aee-5ef0-b081-85127f1a8451" :answer/id #uuid "0df9164a-2aee-5ef0-b081-85127f1a8451" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7}{y}^{2}, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c514f66-29f0-5f0b-bfe0-72c4620d0193" :answer/id #uuid "1c514f66-29f0-5f0b-bfe0-72c4620d0193" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}y, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7040e2bd-4a32-5fec-9df4-e31bdd95ffae" :question/id #uuid "7040e2bd-4a32-5fec-9df4-e31bdd95ffae" :question/math-academy-id "q-145015" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{4}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}[2-\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fcdfbcb7-b6c6-5e73-9143-d0c9ce607525"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fcdfbcb7-b6c6-5e73-9143-d0c9ce607525" :answer-field/id #uuid "fcdfbcb7-b6c6-5e73-9143-d0c9ce607525" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-99847d23-9b4c-53fc-a600-f122a9064fb7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8802a72a-be9c-51d8-a106-ffd3f5b13ac0" "answer-16434b6b-ea07-586f-9f24-fb4740ac451b" "answer-99847d23-9b4c-53fc-a600-f122a9064fb7" "answer-fbb479f7-47d7-58d7-9bbf-b210d2c38e12" "answer-c422b694-0161-5bfa-8a84-689ca1acfe8f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8802a72a-be9c-51d8-a106-ffd3f5b13ac0" :answer/id #uuid "8802a72a-be9c-51d8-a106-ffd3f5b13ac0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16434b6b-ea07-586f-9f24-fb4740ac451b" :answer/id #uuid "16434b6b-ea07-586f-9f24-fb4740ac451b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99847d23-9b4c-53fc-a600-f122a9064fb7" :answer/id #uuid "99847d23-9b4c-53fc-a600-f122a9064fb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbb479f7-47d7-58d7-9bbf-b210d2c38e12" :answer/id #uuid "fbb479f7-47d7-58d7-9bbf-b210d2c38e12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c422b694-0161-5bfa-8a84-689ca1acfe8f" :answer/id #uuid "c422b694-0161-5bfa-8a84-689ca1acfe8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-acc3ecee-2ca3-52a4-a564-fe35d9f4b095" :question/id #uuid "acc3ecee-2ca3-52a4-a564-fe35d9f4b095" :question/math-academy-id "q-142754" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}xy, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{X}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}({x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}xy)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{4}{9}x{y}^{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =({x}^{2}(2)+\\frac{4}{9}x\\cdot {2}^{2})-({x}^{2}(1)+\\frac{4}{9}x\\cdot {1}^{2}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b821f73d-7070-57a0-ab5a-2ac12f5bc93f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b821f73d-7070-57a0-ab5a-2ac12f5bc93f" :answer-field/id #uuid "b821f73d-7070-57a0-ab5a-2ac12f5bc93f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c6feae73-dcc8-57f0-b4da-622fffd1cf65" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3d8a0898-7457-5d87-af4d-85f0fb6d7665" "answer-bea7ae9e-7458-5741-9279-66e4924e7c75" "answer-17aadaf2-4ba7-5796-a001-c0bbe9dcac22" "answer-c6feae73-dcc8-57f0-b4da-622fffd1cf65" "answer-9f32af68-e5ee-55a4-9cfe-8d1f23989236"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d8a0898-7457-5d87-af4d-85f0fb6d7665" :answer/id #uuid "3d8a0898-7457-5d87-af4d-85f0fb6d7665" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x+1}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bea7ae9e-7458-5741-9279-66e4924e7c75" :answer/id #uuid "bea7ae9e-7458-5741-9279-66e4924e7c75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{9}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17aadaf2-4ba7-5796-a001-c0bbe9dcac22" :answer/id #uuid "17aadaf2-4ba7-5796-a001-c0bbe9dcac22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6feae73-dcc8-57f0-b4da-622fffd1cf65" :answer/id #uuid "c6feae73-dcc8-57f0-b4da-622fffd1cf65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f32af68-e5ee-55a4-9cfe-8d1f23989236" :answer/id #uuid "9f32af68-e5ee-55a4-9cfe-8d1f23989236" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a1209ac5-9324-5c4f-8a14-c5d815ce9e79" :question/id #uuid "a1209ac5-9324-5c4f-8a14-c5d815ce9e79" :question/math-academy-id "q-142888" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+xy]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =[(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {1}^{2}+1\\cdot y)-(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}+0\\cdot y)] \\\\  & =y+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y+\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-edc25465-db53-5da9-ab78-ec9a5725f2c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-edc25465-db53-5da9-ab78-ec9a5725f2c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "edc25465-db53-5da9-ab78-ec9a5725f2c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5351eae7-dc6c-5a57-81bb-251115e032a0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b5cfbf8-b34e-5c08-942c-fd1b4c89d51b" "answer-fbad6de2-e944-5d9d-8691-ad17c4fe0fbc" "answer-63acac21-1914-55df-8f46-e1df0c572d17" "answer-5351eae7-dc6c-5a57-81bb-251115e032a0" "answer-ae7225b6-8f8a-507a-869b-7e8fc526e349"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b5cfbf8-b34e-5c08-942c-fd1b4c89d51b" :answer/id #uuid "6b5cfbf8-b34e-5c08-942c-fd1b4c89d51b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbad6de2-e944-5d9d-8691-ad17c4fe0fbc" :answer/id #uuid "fbad6de2-e944-5d9d-8691-ad17c4fe0fbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63acac21-1914-55df-8f46-e1df0c572d17" :answer/id #uuid "63acac21-1914-55df-8f46-e1df0c572d17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y+2, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5351eae7-dc6c-5a57-81bb-251115e032a0" :answer/id #uuid "5351eae7-dc6c-5a57-81bb-251115e032a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y+\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae7225b6-8f8a-507a-869b-7e8fc526e349" :answer/id #uuid "ae7225b6-8f8a-507a-869b-7e8fc526e349" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176261 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(0.2<X<1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.2<X<1) & ={\\int }_{0.2}^{1}{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.2}^{1}(\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}x]}_{0.2}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(1)]-[\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)] \\\\  & =1-0.104 \\\\  & =0.896.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173824 :answer-field/correct 17592186173825 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d033f40-c93e-54e7-8136-01042b0b61b2" :question/id #uuid "6d033f40-c93e-54e7-8136-01042b0b61b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-142967" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y), & 0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}<Y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{12}).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}<Y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{12}) & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /12}{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]}_{0}^{\\pi /12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}[(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{12})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{12})-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+0)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & ≈0.4177.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9c6cde9b-2e7a-54f6-a96c-10b188d72d9e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c6cde9b-2e7a-54f6-a96c-10b188d72d9e" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c6cde9b-2e7a-54f6-a96c-10b188d72d9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b0bf5ad0-1aef-5e73-ad2f-7de86ffb5a37" :answer-field/choices ["answer-39635364-1829-582d-9bac-a7ed3b6b80b2" "answer-11448eff-f99f-5d32-8404-040f21de29d8" "answer-b0bf5ad0-1aef-5e73-ad2f-7de86ffb5a37" "answer-fde49b78-51ae-5a61-b50d-18027829e3e7" "answer-a52fb077-31e9-5727-8a98-141723176b5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39635364-1829-582d-9bac-a7ed3b6b80b2" :answer/id #uuid "39635364-1829-582d-9bac-a7ed3b6b80b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11448eff-f99f-5d32-8404-040f21de29d8" :answer/id #uuid "11448eff-f99f-5d32-8404-040f21de29d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4142" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0bf5ad0-1aef-5e73-ad2f-7de86ffb5a37" :answer/id #uuid "b0bf5ad0-1aef-5e73-ad2f-7de86ffb5a37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4177" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fde49b78-51ae-5a61-b50d-18027829e3e7" :answer/id #uuid "fde49b78-51ae-5a61-b50d-18027829e3e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a52fb077-31e9-5727-8a98-141723176b5f" :answer/id #uuid "a52fb077-31e9-5727-8a98-141723176b5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7071" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-aecec449-e3ae-5803-8a70-f99f6be91bad" :question/id #uuid "aecec449-e3ae-5803-8a70-f99f6be91bad" :question/math-academy-id "q-142911" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(5x+\\frac{y}{5})}, & x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\le 5).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $x\\ge 0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(5x+\\frac{y}{5})}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-5{e}^{-(5x+\\frac{y}{5})}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\infty } \\\\  & =-5(0-{e}^{-(5x+0)}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{-5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{-5x}, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{5}{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}5{e}^{-5x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-5x}]}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-25}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{25}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6b857419-f18b-50b2-bb98-09131889cb3e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6b857419-f18b-50b2-bb98-09131889cb3e" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b857419-f18b-50b2-bb98-09131889cb3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-72270fd2-6992-5f31-97a2-2ca4ee17ded5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-72270fd2-6992-5f31-97a2-2ca4ee17ded5" "answer-968b508d-00d7-5293-968a-76a5988b5ac5" "answer-7ced4ceb-454c-52c6-af4d-6e2ad83dfe18" "answer-b606dc72-4cfc-5e8f-9fe7-991ba2e0b461" "answer-a976e357-0ba9-5d47-9790-62cdf8d6dbdb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72270fd2-6992-5f31-97a2-2ca4ee17ded5" :answer/id #uuid "72270fd2-6992-5f31-97a2-2ca4ee17ded5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{25}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-968b508d-00d7-5293-968a-76a5988b5ac5" :answer/id #uuid "968b508d-00d7-5293-968a-76a5988b5ac5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ced4ceb-454c-52c6-af4d-6e2ad83dfe18" :answer/id #uuid "7ced4ceb-454c-52c6-af4d-6e2ad83dfe18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{25}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b606dc72-4cfc-5e8f-9fe7-991ba2e0b461" :answer/id #uuid "b606dc72-4cfc-5e8f-9fe7-991ba2e0b461" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a976e357-0ba9-5d47-9790-62cdf8d6dbdb" :answer/id #uuid "a976e357-0ba9-5d47-9790-62cdf8d6dbdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{25}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bdb3668b-11de-51d3-b228-d2e5f99dedeb" :question/id #uuid "bdb3668b-11de-51d3-b228-d2e5f99dedeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-142951" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{21}(xy)^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X>1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{21}(xy)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{21}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{21}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{63}({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1) & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}[{3}^{3}-{1}^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-341d4747-e282-5d0e-9b1a-d8cec6a359cd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-341d4747-e282-5d0e-9b1a-d8cec6a359cd" :answer-field/id #uuid "341d4747-e282-5d0e-9b1a-d8cec6a359cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f5587a79-ea8a-50f2-8937-9dd583bde64d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bd15e8ea-65f0-52e8-8cf8-066dd559eb76" "answer-4af6259e-a55c-5863-973f-a60c2eba3557" "answer-320d3cb5-bef1-53b0-95c4-cff9ede43030" "answer-95ffaac9-33b1-5d66-82ac-051de97f1e95" "answer-f5587a79-ea8a-50f2-8937-9dd583bde64d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd15e8ea-65f0-52e8-8cf8-066dd559eb76" :answer/id #uuid "bd15e8ea-65f0-52e8-8cf8-066dd559eb76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4af6259e-a55c-5863-973f-a60c2eba3557" :answer/id #uuid "4af6259e-a55c-5863-973f-a60c2eba3557" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{26}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-320d3cb5-bef1-53b0-95c4-cff9ede43030" :answer/id #uuid "320d3cb5-bef1-53b0-95c4-cff9ede43030" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95ffaac9-33b1-5d66-82ac-051de97f1e95" :answer/id #uuid "95ffaac9-33b1-5d66-82ac-051de97f1e95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5587a79-ea8a-50f2-8937-9dd583bde64d" :answer/id #uuid "f5587a79-ea8a-50f2-8937-9dd583bde64d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{26}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-335726b7-e5f3-5cb6-916f-382cd146373a" :question/id #uuid "335726b7-e5f3-5cb6-916f-382cd146373a" :question/math-academy-id "q-142965" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(\\frac{x}{2}+2y)}, & x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(Y>2).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $y\\ge 0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(\\frac{x}{2}+2y)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-2{e}^{-(\\frac{x}{2}+2y)}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\infty } \\\\  & =-2(0-{e}^{-(0+2y)}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2y}, & y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>2) & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-2y}]}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =(0+{e}^{-4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e40af03a-e8f7-59d9-84b2-010d7a830506"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e40af03a-e8f7-59d9-84b2-010d7a830506" :answer-field/id #uuid "e40af03a-e8f7-59d9-84b2-010d7a830506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-319584c3-1568-5dd4-b6cb-a605a46cc20e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-87cba462-a4d6-545c-b338-05c85b3893b0" "answer-a7c99b52-b19c-5699-807a-a3d706a7ca87" "answer-abe55a60-f081-501a-9966-badc5cf81888" "answer-227e60f3-8280-5cbf-8272-817ecc9418b4" "answer-319584c3-1568-5dd4-b6cb-a605a46cc20e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87cba462-a4d6-545c-b338-05c85b3893b0" :answer/id #uuid "87cba462-a4d6-545c-b338-05c85b3893b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7c99b52-b19c-5699-807a-a3d706a7ca87" :answer/id #uuid "a7c99b52-b19c-5699-807a-a3d706a7ca87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abe55a60-f081-501a-9966-badc5cf81888" :answer/id #uuid "abe55a60-f081-501a-9966-badc5cf81888" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-227e60f3-8280-5cbf-8272-817ecc9418b4" :answer/id #uuid "227e60f3-8280-5cbf-8272-817ecc9418b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-319584c3-1568-5dd4-b6cb-a605a46cc20e" :answer/id #uuid "319584c3-1568-5dd4-b6cb-a605a46cc20e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b503f4b2-2e6a-599e-9f9e-bfcbf92fe455" :question/id #uuid "b503f4b2-2e6a-599e-9f9e-bfcbf92fe455" :question/math-academy-id "q-142710" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with a joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{3},\\,0\\le 3y\\le x\\le 3.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le 3y\\le x\\le 3\\}.$\n\n![](images/54/54c803be9ecc7873f2624fc9d083997039cb651c11cc38eff6fa561ec064b7a5.png)\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{3y}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{3y}^{3}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=3y}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {3}^{3}+3\\cdot {y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}(3y)^{3}-3y\\cdot {y}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[9+3{y}^{2}-12{y}^{3}] \\\\  & =3+{y}^{2}-4{y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3+{y}^{2}-4{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8f4e6988-a890-5061-983b-4ccf67591ee4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8f4e6988-a890-5061-983b-4ccf67591ee4" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f4e6988-a890-5061-983b-4ccf67591ee4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d5462deb-905b-5315-b5e7-9ee7d87bb3b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9fd12cd1-d9b6-5434-b061-5a342e650a92" "answer-8b2b6b61-00a6-5cd5-b748-9e114f816504" "answer-d5462deb-905b-5315-b5e7-9ee7d87bb3b0" "answer-2fd49525-ce7b-5de7-bb4b-853ca8c7b51d" "answer-5f91b3ea-874f-54c6-9b5a-27d6749d139c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fd12cd1-d9b6-5434-b061-5a342e650a92" :answer/id #uuid "9fd12cd1-d9b6-5434-b061-5a342e650a92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1+3{y}^{2}-4{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b2b6b61-00a6-5cd5-b748-9e114f816504" :answer/id #uuid "8b2b6b61-00a6-5cd5-b748-9e114f816504" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1+{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5462deb-905b-5315-b5e7-9ee7d87bb3b0" :answer/id #uuid "d5462deb-905b-5315-b5e7-9ee7d87bb3b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3+{y}^{2}-4{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fd49525-ce7b-5de7-bb4b-853ca8c7b51d" :answer/id #uuid "2fd49525-ce7b-5de7-bb4b-853ca8c7b51d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6{y}^{2}-3{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f91b3ea-874f-54c6-9b5a-27d6749d139c" :answer/id #uuid "5f91b3ea-874f-54c6-9b5a-27d6749d139c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176364 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with a joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\pi {x}^{2}},\\,{y}^{2}+1\\le x.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{y}^{2}+1\\le x\\}.$\n\n![](images/0a/0a75ec87c30ea5708201cb76816ea3a806648cec197195994cafbe9d9cf588d1.png)\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $-\\infty <y<\\infty $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{{y}^{2}+1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\pi {x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{{y}^{2}+1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{{y}^{2}+1}^{b}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{x={y}^{2}+1}^{x=b} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{b}-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }[0-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi ({y}^{2}+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{\\pi ({y}^{2}+1)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186174442 :answer-field/correct "answer-0e1c2488-6f19-5f75-8228-75b61035e030" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0e1c2488-6f19-5f75-8228-75b61035e030" "answer-82eb8742-36e7-5ffd-a6f6-69aaa4ab4057" "answer-1961d4db-fe56-563a-9283-1c81c4dc846c" "answer-95a54a82-53ef-52bd-a12a-f81380aaff75" "answer-9558bd26-9177-5a95-ae61-67abc43f1a3e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e1c2488-6f19-5f75-8228-75b61035e030" :answer/id #uuid "0e1c2488-6f19-5f75-8228-75b61035e030" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{\\pi ({y}^{2}+1)}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82eb8742-36e7-5ffd-a6f6-69aaa4ab4057" :answer/id #uuid "82eb8742-36e7-5ffd-a6f6-69aaa4ab4057" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\pi }}\\,{e}^{-{y}^{2}}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1961d4db-fe56-563a-9283-1c81c4dc846c" :answer/id #uuid "1961d4db-fe56-563a-9283-1c81c4dc846c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95a54a82-53ef-52bd-a12a-f81380aaff75" :answer/id #uuid "95a54a82-53ef-52bd-a12a-f81380aaff75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{2}{\\pi (4{y}^{4}+1)}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9558bd26-9177-5a95-ae61-67abc43f1a3e" :answer/id #uuid "9558bd26-9177-5a95-ae61-67abc43f1a3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)={e}^{-{y}^{2}}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-076df80a-4584-5238-8a7e-ff37062cbf3b" :question/id #uuid "076df80a-4584-5238-8a7e-ff37062cbf3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-142857" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{X}(x)$ of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ g(x), & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[{y}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =({1}^{2}-0) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}{f}_{X}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}1\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =[u]_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =x-0 \\\\  & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${F}_{X}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ x, & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $g(x)=x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-efcde246-3b99-5c3b-9257-5e8e1919f2e1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-efcde246-3b99-5c3b-9257-5e8e1919f2e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "efcde246-3b99-5c3b-9257-5e8e1919f2e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-471383ca-dfca-562f-871b-65f52c3bf25c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-141b8f61-deff-5934-b9c3-910770639c5b" "answer-f61eda3e-11f8-5e7b-9353-d73bdfe137ad" "answer-471383ca-dfca-562f-871b-65f52c3bf25c" "answer-f1599fb6-22fd-570f-a8e0-dcdc16c9cddc" "answer-35b1ba0b-b624-5ab8-b04e-b638b43bbe11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-141b8f61-deff-5934-b9c3-910770639c5b" :answer/id #uuid "141b8f61-deff-5934-b9c3-910770639c5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f61eda3e-11f8-5e7b-9353-d73bdfe137ad" :answer/id #uuid "f61eda3e-11f8-5e7b-9353-d73bdfe137ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-471383ca-dfca-562f-871b-65f52c3bf25c" :answer/id #uuid "471383ca-dfca-562f-871b-65f52c3bf25c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1599fb6-22fd-570f-a8e0-dcdc16c9cddc" :answer/id #uuid "f1599fb6-22fd-570f-a8e0-dcdc16c9cddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35b1ba0b-b624-5ab8-b04e-b638b43bbe11" :answer/id #uuid "35b1ba0b-b624-5ab8-b04e-b638b43bbe11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b66f8317-7401-5c42-a057-174f43015e08" :question/id #uuid "b66f8317-7401-5c42-a057-174f43015e08" :question/math-academy-id "q-142924" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}, & x\\ge 1,\\,y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{X}(x)$ of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ g(x), & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $x\\ge 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{b}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{y=1}^{y=b} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }[1-\\frac{1}{b}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $X$ for $x\\ge 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}{f}_{X}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{u}]}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-1}{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${F}_{X}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ \\frac{x-1}{x}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $g(x)=\\frac{x-1}{x}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9b5eb91d-c108-5a2b-99e3-c07f16397e3a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9b5eb91d-c108-5a2b-99e3-c07f16397e3a" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b5eb91d-c108-5a2b-99e3-c07f16397e3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c9e5ae14-8d9d-5fd7-be35-533fed06278b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a48b4c7-e269-5b07-a4ea-37ff96fee042" "answer-19e05135-dc72-54d1-a265-7303f0c55750" "answer-c9e5ae14-8d9d-5fd7-be35-533fed06278b" "answer-772175ea-626c-579e-9d22-f7b5ba8cba19" "answer-b8329249-ead1-5e17-95ed-e5b59ee76c7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a48b4c7-e269-5b07-a4ea-37ff96fee042" :answer/id #uuid "2a48b4c7-e269-5b07-a4ea-37ff96fee042" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19e05135-dc72-54d1-a265-7303f0c55750" :answer/id #uuid "19e05135-dc72-54d1-a265-7303f0c55750" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9e5ae14-8d9d-5fd7-be35-533fed06278b" :answer/id #uuid "c9e5ae14-8d9d-5fd7-be35-533fed06278b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-772175ea-626c-579e-9d22-f7b5ba8cba19" :answer/id #uuid "772175ea-626c-579e-9d22-f7b5ba8cba19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8329249-ead1-5e17-95ed-e5b59ee76c7b" :answer/id #uuid "b8329249-ead1-5e17-95ed-e5b59ee76c7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-74d58075-0369-56a0-b633-ba74268879be" :question/id #uuid "74d58075-0369-56a0-b633-ba74268879be" :question/math-academy-id "q-142916" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y\\sqrt{x}}{9}, & 0\\le x\\le 9,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{Y}(y)$ of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & y<0 \\\\ g(y), & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & y>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(y)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{9}\\frac{y\\sqrt{x}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{9}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{9}{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}]}_{x=0}^{x=9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{27}{[{x}^{3/2}]}_{x=0}^{x=9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{27}({9}^{3/2}-{0}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{27}(27-0) \\\\  & =2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{f}_{Y}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}2u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[{u}^{2}]}_{0}^{y} \\\\  & ={y}^{2}-0 \\\\  & ={y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${F}_{Y}(y)$ is\n\n$$\n{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & y<0 \\\\ {y}^{2}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & y>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $g(y)={y}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9146ede4-3856-5d3a-8193-cdcf33cf5f1c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9146ede4-3856-5d3a-8193-cdcf33cf5f1c" :answer-field/id #uuid "9146ede4-3856-5d3a-8193-cdcf33cf5f1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9c74adee-37f0-5906-921a-264e40407fe1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1a53314f-f55e-5de3-9361-255122ecd28d" "answer-1f7ed870-0b8d-550d-abc6-3a5002277034" "answer-59076299-fa05-510b-bc19-29ea93c3586f" "answer-9c74adee-37f0-5906-921a-264e40407fe1" "answer-20349e86-f87d-5afc-84ce-b2382a2a6350"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a53314f-f55e-5de3-9361-255122ecd28d" :answer/id #uuid "1a53314f-f55e-5de3-9361-255122ecd28d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f7ed870-0b8d-550d-abc6-3a5002277034" :answer/id #uuid "1f7ed870-0b8d-550d-abc6-3a5002277034" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}^{3/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59076299-fa05-510b-bc19-29ea93c3586f" :answer/id #uuid "59076299-fa05-510b-bc19-29ea93c3586f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c74adee-37f0-5906-921a-264e40407fe1" :answer/id #uuid "9c74adee-37f0-5906-921a-264e40407fe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20349e86-f87d-5afc-84ce-b2382a2a6350" :answer/id #uuid "20349e86-f87d-5afc-84ce-b2382a2a6350" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4107781e-c996-571c-b9f1-cc16eec90a01" :question/id #uuid "4107781e-c996-571c-b9f1-cc16eec90a01" :question/math-academy-id "q-142861" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+y}, & x\\le 0,\\,y\\le 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{Y}(y)$ of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}g(y), & y\\le 0 \\\\ 1 & y>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(y)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $y\\le 0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{y}{lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{b}^{0}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{y}{lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }{[{e}^{x}]}_{b}^{0} \\\\  & ={e}^{y}{lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }(1-{e}^{b}) \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $Y$ for $y\\le 0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{f}_{Y}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{b}^{y}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }{[{e}^{u}]}_{b}^{y} \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }({e}^{y}-{e}^{b}) \\\\  & ={e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${F}_{Y}(y)$ is\n\n$$\n{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y}, & y\\le 0 \\\\ 1 & y>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $g(y)={e}^{y}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-057d939c-b8eb-5a5d-bd62-0bb22aaeb85f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-057d939c-b8eb-5a5d-bd62-0bb22aaeb85f" :answer-field/id #uuid "057d939c-b8eb-5a5d-bd62-0bb22aaeb85f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3720d3c5-7d4d-5275-98de-8c62924defdc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-080ba9b9-8963-507d-b891-91fccbf687c0" "answer-e9e9020e-860d-5a4e-a5c5-8098b6ef2473" "answer-6d1d0f0d-8129-5494-8892-c2b298041668" "answer-3720d3c5-7d4d-5275-98de-8c62924defdc" "answer-28302a4c-381c-5184-8bf7-1a2de35cc31a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-080ba9b9-8963-507d-b891-91fccbf687c0" :answer/id #uuid "080ba9b9-8963-507d-b891-91fccbf687c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{e}^{-y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9e9020e-860d-5a4e-a5c5-8098b6ef2473" :answer/id #uuid "e9e9020e-860d-5a4e-a5c5-8098b6ef2473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{e}^{-{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d1d0f0d-8129-5494-8892-c2b298041668" :answer/id #uuid "6d1d0f0d-8129-5494-8892-c2b298041668" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3720d3c5-7d4d-5275-98de-8c62924defdc" :answer/id #uuid "3720d3c5-7d4d-5275-98de-8c62924defdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28302a4c-381c-5184-8bf7-1a2de35cc31a" :answer/id #uuid "28302a4c-381c-5184-8bf7-1a2de35cc31a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-31433c7d-56df-5a56-80c3-21c7e39be82f" :question/id #uuid "31433c7d-56df-5a56-80c3-21c7e39be82f" :question/math-academy-id "q-142923" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{(x+y)^{3}}, & x\\ge 1,\\,y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{X}(x)$ of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ g(x), & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $x\\ge 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{(x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{b}\\frac{4}{(x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{b}(x+y)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{2}(x+y)^{-2}]}_{y=1}^{y=b} \\\\  & =-2{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}]}_{y=1}^{y=b} \\\\  & =-2{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{(x+b)^{2}}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(x+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $X$ for $x\\ge 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}{f}_{X}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{2}{(u+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{1}{(u+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2{[-\\frac{1}{u+1}]}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =2[\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{x+1}] \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{x+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-1}{x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${F}_{X}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ \\frac{x-1}{x+1}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $g(x)=\\frac{x-1}{x+1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7592e58e-c6d2-57f8-87f1-5cf59d6709fe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7592e58e-c6d2-57f8-87f1-5cf59d6709fe" :answer-field/id #uuid "7592e58e-c6d2-57f8-87f1-5cf59d6709fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7e8bf4a0-5dfd-5230-8dc4-539d957d5aa3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-91cec410-3544-5b99-84ab-6aa46c4443e7" "answer-b4e7a5c1-ac85-558b-941d-74d5104f775a" "answer-7e8bf4a0-5dfd-5230-8dc4-539d957d5aa3" "answer-dcf8e657-8c89-50bd-98b0-b327d64295c1" "answer-657be62f-e6cf-5e98-b0fe-061ed0c317ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91cec410-3544-5b99-84ab-6aa46c4443e7" :answer/id #uuid "91cec410-3544-5b99-84ab-6aa46c4443e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4e7a5c1-ac85-558b-941d-74d5104f775a" :answer/id #uuid "b4e7a5c1-ac85-558b-941d-74d5104f775a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(x+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e8bf4a0-5dfd-5230-8dc4-539d957d5aa3" :answer/id #uuid "7e8bf4a0-5dfd-5230-8dc4-539d957d5aa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcf8e657-8c89-50bd-98b0-b327d64295c1" :answer/id #uuid "dcf8e657-8c89-50bd-98b0-b327d64295c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-657be62f-e6cf-5e98-b0fe-061ed0c317ce" :answer/id #uuid "657be62f-e6cf-5e98-b0fe-061ed0c317ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177001 :tutorial/content "We've seen how to construct the marginal mass functions for two discrete random variables from their joint probability mass function. We now wish to formulate analogous definitions when our random variables are continuous. \n\nFirst, recall that if $f(x,y)$ is the joint PMF of the *discrete* random variables $X$ and $Y$ with supports $S_X$ and $S_Y$, respectively, then\n\n- the marginal mass function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_X(x)  = \\displaystyle \\sum\\limits_{y \\in S_Y} f(x,y)\n$$\n\n- and the marginal mass function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_Y(y)  = \\displaystyle \\sum\\limits_{x \\in S_X} f(x,y).\n$$\n\nNow suppose that $X$ and $Y$ are *continuous* random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y).$  \n\n- The **marginal density function** of $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf_X(x) = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}y.\n$$\n\n- The **marginal density function** of $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf_Y(y) = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} f (x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe sometimes refer to a marginal density function as a **marginal probability density function** (or **marginal PDF**).\n\nIt's helpful to appreciate the analogy between the discrete and continuous cases as this often helps us to remember their definitions. In summary:\n\n- To convert from discrete to continuous, we turn sums into integrals.\n\n- When we compute $f_X$ in the discrete case, we sum over all possible values of $Y.$ In the continuous case, we integrate with respect to $y.$\n\n- When we compute $f_Y$ in the discrete case, we sum over all possible values of $X.$ In the continuous case, we integrate with respect to $x.$\n\nLet's now see a concrete example of how to compute a marginal density function." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177056 :tutorial/content "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n![](images/e2/e229c78e51036e7fb7b7e9345bbe4f2ede5704032d65d2581b53c8a5f59ef603.svg)\n\nLet's find the expression for the marginal density function $f_X(x)$ of $X.$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\leq x \\leq 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[{x}^{2}\\cdot 1+\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}]-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot [0] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3{x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_X(x)$ is given by\n\n![](images/e8/e8eb5c2dedf51c1b232af9e2dd6a4eb12621daaa78ab34f18a46e26a9a6d2887.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177057 :tutorial/content "Recall that the cumulative distribution function (or CDF) of a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X\\leq x) = \\int_{-\\infty}^x f(t)\\,\\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nNow suppose we know the marginal distributions $f_X(x)$ and $f_Y(y)$ of the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y.$\n\nThen we can define the **marginal cumulative distribution functions** (or **marginal CDFs**) of $X$ and $Y$ analogously as follows:\n\n- The marginal CDF of $X,$ denoted $F_X(x),$ is given by\n\n$$\nF_X(x) = P(X\\leq x) = \\int_{-\\infty}^x f_X(t)\\,\\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n- The marginal CDF of $Y,$ denoted $F_Y(y),$ is given by\n\n$$\nF_Y(y) = P(Y\\leq y) = \\int_{-\\infty}^y f_Y(t)\\,\\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nLet's see an example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176153 :activity/expected-seconds 1140.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
